meta {
  name: Collect Order Group
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/collect-group
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "sampleIds": ["{{orderSampleId}}"],
    "print": false
  }
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
  test("order returned", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().data).to.have.property("id");
  });
}

docs {
  Collect a whole **group** of the order's accession samples at once — the
  group-wise counterpart of `Collect Order Item`, backing the Product Overview
  modal's grouped Test Details (Collect / Collect & Print on a group's flat
  `sampleIds`).

  Body:

  - `sampleIds[]` (required, non-empty UUIDs) — a group's accession sample ids
    (from `44 Get Order Grouped Samples` → `groups[].sampleIds`).
  - `print` (optional) — mirrors "Collect & Print": also assign a barcode to any
    sample in the group that lacks one (`BAR-#####-A`).

  Every collectable sample in the set (NEW / HOLD / REPEAT) is transitioned to
  COLLECTED in one tenant-scoped transaction (an `AccessionStatusHistory` row is
  appended), and — because a sample is one physical tube shared by several tests —
  every sibling order item on a transitioned sample is stamped
  `collectedAt`/`collectedBy` too. Returns the refreshed, fully-composed order.

  Idempotent: samples already past NEW/HOLD/REPEAT are skipped (no
  `INVALID_SAMPLE_TRANSITION`); a repeat call on an all-collected group is a
  no-op. 404 `ORDER_NOT_FOUND` if the order is missing/other-tenant.
}
